  "guid": "848BB160847C11EAB53C112B1A2624CA",
  "guidelines": "**General Tips**\n\n1. We generally use low split ratios of 1:3 or 1:2 with our organoid cultures. We will also passage to the same or a lower number of wells if organoids are not growing (see troubleshooting below).\n1. We use 5 ml Eppendorf tubes to help with sterility. However, if you do not have access to these tubes any alternative sterile tubes of appropriate volume can be used.\n1. Cold PBS is helpful for resolving some pelleting issues (see toubleshooting below). Therefore it is useful to keep a bottle of PBS in fridge.\n\n\n**Reasons for passaging organoids**\n  \n[Reasons for passaging.png]](https://content.protocols.io/public/417fb9cd53044f7c6eb3e93de0e730f2c4aafce8332e96e3c04a19c0dd149ad8/b63ebc2j7.png)\n \n**Troubleshooting**\n[Troubleshooting.png]](https://content.protocols.io/public/417fb9cd53044f7c6eb3e93de0e730f2c4aafce8332e96e3c04a19c0dd149ad8/b6trbc2j7.png)\n \n \n",
